Source: openssl-fips@FIPSVER@-upstream
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: OpenSSL Packages <openssl-packages@openssl.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 12~), perl
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://openssl-library.org

Package: openssl-fips@FIPSVER@-upstream
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenSSL FIPS provider @FIPSVER@ (upstream build)
 The OpenSSL FIPS provider module (fips.so) built from source release
 @FIPSVER@ with `enable-fips` and nothing else, installed at
 /opt/openssl/fips/@FIPSVER@/fips.so — a stream-independent path, so one
 module can serve any installed OpenSSL stream.
 .
 Activate it for a stream on the deployment machine, e.g.:
   /opt/openssl/4.0/bin/openssl-fips-enable @FIPSVER@
 .
 Whether this source version holds a NIST CMVP certificate is reported by
 "openssl-fips-enable list"; a module without one enforces approved-only
 algorithms but does not make an installation FIPS 140-3 compliant.
